' purpose: Development diagnostics, saved explanations and host-runner PASS never grant F9 readiness.
' covers: mise.toml
' covers: tooling/native-ingress/f9-diagnose.mjs
' covers: tooling/native-ingress/f9-requirements.mjs
' covers: tooling/native-ingress/f9-summary.mjs
' covers: tooling/native-ingress/f9-explain.mjs
' covers: tooling/native-ingress/f9-verify-sbx.mjs
' covers: tooling/native-ingress/tests/f9-diagnose.test.mjs
' covers: tooling/native-ingress/tests/f9-explain.test.mjs
' covers: tooling/native-ingress/tests/f9-verify-sbx.test.mjs
' covers: tooling/native-ingress/F9-DIAGNOSTIC.md
' covers: tooling/sbx-dev/stages.mjs
' covers: tooling/sbx-dev/tests/stages.test.mjs
' covers: tooling/sbx-dev/acquire-tools.mjs
' covers: tooling/sbx-dev/check-bundle.mjs
' covers: tooling/sbx-dev/tests/acquire-tools.test.mjs
' covers: tooling/sbx-dev/tests/setup.test.mjs
' related: _spec/tooling/sbx-dev/preparation-workflow.puml
' related: _spec/tooling/bun-first-party-tooling.puml
' related: _spec/_plans/native-ingress-rust-first-full-plan-packet.md
' status: Host verification AUTHORED; offline suites 118 PASS / 0 FAIL; scoped host-helper code/spec and planned-publication review READY, no findings; real guest NOT_RUN; Gate0 OPEN; F9/training false.
' source: Mise documentation observations supplied by the lead; no fetch in this pass.
' reference: https://mise.jdx.dev/configuration/settings.html#auto_install
' reference: https://mise.jdx.dev/tasks/task-configuration.html#raw-args
' note-register: DIAG right cancellation FK 12.1; DIAG/GUEST crash FK 12.7; DIAG/GATES authority FK 12.3.
' note-register: OP/VERIFY approval FK 11.3; BOUNDED/GUEST deadline FK 10.7; MISE configuration FK 12.5.
' note-register: GUEST/MISE privacy FK 10.2; VERIFY/GATES authority FK 11.9.
' FK counts: approval W26/S48/N2; deadline W24/S44/N2; configuration W23/S46/N2.
' FK counts: privacy W24/S43/N2; authority W25/S48/N2; W=words, S=syllables, N=sentences.
' FK syllables: hand-counted English; CLI=3, F9=2, Gate0=3, KUnit=3, G1=2.
@startuml f9-diagnostic
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title Development diagnostics, saved explanation and host verification / Gate0 remains OPEN
actor Executor as OP
participant "dev:sbx:create\nexisting helper" as CREATE <<host>>
participant "f9:diagnose\nBun supervisor" as DIAG <<app>>
participant "Named development sbx" as VM <<host>>
participant "Fixed guest timeout + shell" as GUEST <<app>>
participant "f9-requirements.mjs\nstatic catalogue (44 current rows)" as GATES <<db>>
participant "f9-explain.mjs\nf9:explain read-only CLI" as EXPLAIN <<app>>
participant "f9-summary.mjs\npure formatter" as SUMMARY <<app>>
database "Exact requested report leaf" as REPORT <<db>>
participant "f9-verify-sbx.mjs\nf9:verify-sbx host CLI" as VERIFY <<app>>
participant "f9-diagnose.mjs\nrunBounded host supervisor" as BOUNDED <<app>>
participant "mise\nexisting guest f9:explain task" as MISE <<host>>

OP -> CREATE : separately approved creation attempt
CREATE --> OP : confirmed name / ambiguous state
OP -> DIAG : --plan: print fixed scope only
DIAG --> OP : no sbx invocation; STOP
OP -> DIAG : separately approved named diagnostic
DIAG -> VM : ls -q (10s, 64KiB)
VM --> DIAG : complete unique-name observation
DIAG -> VM : policy ls --wide NAME (10s, 64KiB)
VM --> DIAG : bounded policy bytes
DIAG -> GUEST : exec NAME timeout 8s + kill 1s
GUEST --> DIAG : fixed capability fields (20s, 16KiB)
DIAG -> GATES : list N1-N10, G1-G5 and remaining gates
GATES --> DIAG : BLOCKED; verifiers not connected
DIAG --> OP : diagnostic completion != readiness
DIAG --> OP : result STOP; exit 2; trainingReady false
DIAG --> OP : original JSON stdout and schema unchanged

note over DIAG, GUEST
  No create/copy/build/test/reset/remove
  Raw policy and errors stay off the terminal
end note
note left of DIAG
  graceMilliseconds: integer 0..1000
  Leaf default 0: immediate KILL; <=2s reap
  Validator/diagnostic supervisors: 1000
  SIGINT/SIGTERM handlers registered pre-spawn
end note
note right of DIAG
  Cooperative cancellation gives the nested Bun
  helper time to stop its detached CLI group.
  The outer wrapper escalates to KILL after one
  second and allows two seconds to reap without
  accepting failed or interrupted outcomes.
end note
note over DIAG, GUEST
  Helper signal handlers propagate cancellation
  to the detached CLI group before normal exit.
  A helper crash can bypass that cooperation,
  so bounded host cleanup cannot prove that
  every descendant or guest process stopped.
end note
note over DIAG, GATES
  Probe results are observations, not proof that
  independent F9 gates have passed.
  Gate0 and separate approvals remain required
  for capture, KUnit, G1 and Native workloads,
  which this diagnostic never runs.
end note

group Offline saved-report explanation: no fresh observations
  OP -> EXPLAIN : mise run f9:explain -- --report <normalized-absolute-path>
  note right of EXPLAIN
    Bun --no-env-file --no-install
    Independent task; auto_install=false
  end note
  EXPLAIN -> EXPLAIN : main(argv): --report PATH or --report=PATH; no other arguments
  EXPLAIN -> REPORT : readDiagnosticReport(path): normalized absolute; control-free; <=4096 UTF-8 bytes\nO_RDONLY | O_NOFOLLOW | O_NONBLOCK on exact requested leaf
  REPORT --> EXPLAIN : same descriptor: regular file; size<=128KiB\nBigInt metadata before/after
  EXPLAIN -> EXPLAIN : read <=128KiB+1 sentinel; accept <=128KiB; bytes=stable size\nunchanged dev/ino/size/mtimeNs/ctimeNs/mode/nlink; always close descriptor
  EXPLAIN -> SUMMARY : formatDiagnosticSummary(report)\nf9-live-diagnostic-v1; DEVELOPMENT_RECONNAISSANCE_ONLY
  SUMMARY -> GATES : compare all rows in catalogue order: id, source, nextStep\ncount=requirements.length (44 currently)
  GATES --> SUMMARY : exact static catalogue; BLOCKED / NOT_RUN / verifier=null
  SUMMARY -> SUMMARY : diagnosticComplete=true; liveGuestObserved=true; four known PASS probes\nif present: cliSucceeded=true, outcome=EXIT, code=0, signal=null\nresult=STOP; f9Qualified=false; trainingReady=false
  SUMMARY -> SUMMARY : safe target; exact guest capability vocabulary\nnever print opaque policy, reasons, errors or private fields
  alt structurally complete, consistent retained live-v1 report
    SUMMARY --> EXPLAIN : F9_NOT_ASSESSED: count/count BLOCKED; NOT_RUN / verifier=null\nnot failed tests; recorded PATH tools PRESENT/MISSING; seeded pair separate\nf9:diagnose exit 2; f9:explain exit 0 (presentation only; no F9 authority)
    EXPLAIN --> OP : stdout: SAVED_REPORT_ONLY + explanation\nSTOP; f9Qualified=false; trainingReady=false\nstderr empty; exit 0
  else invalid arguments/read/schema, plan, incomplete or inconsistent fields
    EXPLAIN --> OP : stdout empty; fixed stderr refusal\nSTOP; trainingReady=false; exit 2
  end
  note over EXPLAIN, REPORT
    Read only the requested report leaf
    Ancestor symlinks allowed; leaf links refused
    No refs, siblings, VM calls or subprocesses
    No network, writes or new approvals
  end note
  note right of EXPLAIN
    exit 0: presentation only, not qualification
    No fresh or authenticated live evidence
  end note
  note over EXPLAIN, SUMMARY
    Saved probe results describe a past guest
    observation, not current authenticated state.
    Consistent report fields cannot prove that
    setup actually completed or that independent
    F9 requirements have passed.
  end note
  note right of SUMMARY
    The seeded check tests both executable paths
    as one pair, apart from recorded PATH results.
    If that pair is unavailable, either tool may
    still exist; presence proves no version,
    provenance or runtime behavior.
  end note
end

group Host-side verification contract: offline fake-provider tests PASS; real guest NOT_RUN
  OP -> VERIFY : mise run f9:verify-sbx --sbx SBX --name NAME --repo REPO --report REPORT\nexactly one of --plan / --confirm-dev-verification\nBun --no-env-file --no-install; raw_args=true; no task dependencies/tools/env
  VERIFY -> VERIFY : parseVerificationArgs: unique known options; no positionals\nlexically normalized absolute UTF-8 paths; no controls/trailing slash; <=4096 bytes\nNAME is literal [A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9_.-]{0,63}; no discovery
  alt invalid arguments or ambiguous mode
    VERIFY --> OP : sanitized STOP; exit 2; no executable inspection/provider call
  else plan mode (--plan)
    VERIFY --> OP : PLAN_ONLY; exit 0; frozen argv/settings only\nno executable metadata checks or provider queries; not permission\nGate0 OPEN; f9Qualified=false; trainingReady=false
  else execution acknowledgement (--confirm-dev-verification)
    note over OP, VERIFY
  The confirmation flag acknowledges a request,
  not permission to execute a live command.
  Fresh approval must bind the chosen controller,
  guest paths and configuration before use.
    end note
    VERIFY -> VERIFY : inspectExecutable(SBX): regular executable non-link leaf\nlstat before/after + access(X_OK); no body/hash/version read
    alt executable checks fail
      VERIFY --> OP : sanitized STOP / INVALID_EXECUTABLE; exit 2; no spawn
    else executable checks pass: not provider identity or execution authority
      VERIFY -> BOUNDED : one fixed argv; milliseconds=35000; cap=65536 combined bytes\ngraceMilliseconds=1000; existing bounded host-group termination/reaping
      BOUNDED -> VM : SBX exec NAME /usr/bin/timeout --kill-after=1s 25s\n/bin/sh -c FIXED sh REPO REPORT; exec may start a stopped VM\nno ls/policy/create/copy/install/provision/cleanup/retry
      VM -> GUEST : fixed script; repo/report are quoted positional values\nalready provisioned approved guest repo/config/imports/report; no host report read/copy
      note over BOUNDED, GUEST
  Terminating the controller cannot establish
  that a guest process has stopped.
  The guest deadline limits a requested command,
  but supplies no independent quiescence proof.
      end note
      GUEST -> GUEST : emit F9_SBX_EXPLAIN_V1; command -v all fifteen names\nemit every ordered TOOL_name=PRESENT|MISSING field
      note right of GUEST
  PATH only: command -v, in this order
  tar sha256sum timeout gpgv patch make clang
  ld.bfd readelf node rustc cargo zig mise bun
  No version/build queries or seeded-path credit
      end note
      alt any PATH tool missing
        GUEST --> BOUNDED : all fifteen tool fields; RESULT=TOOLS_MISSING; exit 2\nno mise invocation
      else all tools present but cd REPO fails
        GUEST --> BOUNDED : RESULT=REPO_UNAVAILABLE; exit 2; no mise invocation
      else all tools present and cd "$1" succeeds
        GUEST -> MISE : MISE_AUTO_INSTALL=false mise run f9:explain --report "$2"\n>/dev/null 2>&1; raw-args form without an added separator
        note right of MISE
  Disabling automatic installation does not
  confine configuration hooks or plugin startup.
  The operator must approve those guest effects
  before the requested task runs.
        end note
        MISE -> EXPLAIN : existing guest task/helper and approved source imports\nroot auto_install=false and tool pins unchanged\ninstalled Mise forwarding/setting behavior remains UNTESTED
        EXPLAIN -> REPORT : read only existing guest report through unchanged explainer API
        REPORT --> EXPLAIN : retained diagnostic fields, not fresh or authenticated observations
        EXPLAIN --> MISE : formatting exit 0 can legitimately describe a STOP report\ninvalid arguments/read/report return exit 2
        MISE --> GUEST : task status only; stdout/stderr discarded
        note over GUEST, MISE
  Task output is discarded before the guest
  emits the final protocol result.
  This separation prevents task logs from posing
  as protocol evidence of success.
        end note
        GUEST --> BOUNDED : RESULT=EXPLAIN_SUCCEEDED with exit 0\nor RESULT=EXPLAIN_FAILED with exit 2
      end
      BOUNDED --> VERIFY : bounded stdout/stderr, outcome, code, signal or execution failure
      VERIFY -> VERIFY : parseGuestVerification: exact marker + fifteen ordered unique tool fields\n+ one allowed RESULT row + final newline; missing/result consistency\nno duplicate/reordered/unknown/extra authority fields
      alt EXPLAIN_SUCCEEDED, all tools PRESENT, EXIT, ok=true, code=0, signal=null, stderr empty, within cap
        VERIFY --> OP : development result PASS; exit 0\nallToolsAvailable=true; explanationSucceeded=true\nGate0 OPEN; f9Qualified=false; trainingReady=false
      else missing/repo/explainer failure, malformed/crossed protocol, nonzero, signal, overflow, stderr or spawn error
        VERIFY --> OP : sanitized STOP; exit 2; no raw provider stdout/stderr/error names\nGate0 OPEN; f9Qualified=false; trainingReady=false; no retry
      end
    end
    note over VERIFY, GATES
  Tool presence and report formatting do not
  prove source identity or native behavior.
  Independent Gate0 acceptance remains required,
  and this runner grants no such authority.
    end note
  end
end
@enduml
